Z||000000||Splash||11-25-1999||01:53 PM||||<BR>OK guy's, I need some help with my <BR>clutch..... In neutral when I push <BR>down on the clutch pedal there is <BR>a squealling noise coming from the <BR>engine, I beleive this may be the <BR>clutch release bearing, If so what <BR>are my options for a quick turn <BR>around to keep it on the road? <BR>This is my only work car.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-25-1999||07:02 PM||||Only in neutral? You sure you just can't hear it other times because it being drowned out? <P>A bearing would likely make noise in all gears. It could either be the throwout, disk drag, or the crank if it's thrust plate is near dead. (The thrust bearing for the crank is part of the mains.) Your most likely are the throwout or disk failure. You won't know untill it's appart.||||reg||1
